meta {
  name: Object on v1.1
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1.1/objects/:objectId
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  objectId: 45734
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 404
}

docs {
  Only search moved to `v1.1`. The same id that answers on `v1` is a 404
  here, which is why the version is written per endpoint in
  `collection_remote_repository.dart` and not once in the base URL.

  Moving the object request to `v1.1` would not show an error: the app
  takes a 404 on an object to mean "nothing to show", so every search
  would end in "Nothing to show yet".
}
